---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Project Configuration — IonPath" current="/guides/ion-config/">
  <div class="animate-fade-in-up">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-2">Project Configuration</h1>
    <p class="text-text-secondary mb-8">The <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">ion.config.json</code> file defines your project name, enabled features, and code generation targets.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-12 animate-fade-in-up-delay-1">

    <section>
      <h2 id="full-example" class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Full Example</h2>
      <div class="code-block text-[13px]">
        <pre>{'{'}
  "name": "MyProject",
  "features": ["std"],
  "modules": {'{'}
    "auth": "../shared/auth-contracts"
  {'}'},
  "generators": {'{'}
    "dotnet": {'{'}
      "features": ["models", "client", "server"],
      "outputs": "./"
    {'}'},
    "browser": {'{'}
      "outputFile": "./client.generated.ts"
    {'}'}
  {'}'}
{'}'}</pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="name" class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">name</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3"><strong>Required.</strong> The project name. Used as the module identifier in generated code and schema lock files.</p>
      <div class="code-block text-[13px]">
        <pre>"name": "MyContracts"</pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="features" class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">features</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3"><strong>Required.</strong> An array of feature modules to enable. Available features:</p>
      <div class="type-grid">
        <div class="type-grid-header">
          <span>Feature</span>
          <span>Description</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-keyword">std</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Standard library — includes all primitive types, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Maybe&lt;T&gt;</code>, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Array&lt;T&gt;</code>, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Partial&lt;T&gt;</code></span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-keyword">orleans</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Microsoft Orleans integration — grain-aware code generation</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-3">The list is closed — any other string is rejected when the config is read. A file can assert that it needs one of these with the <a href="/guides/directives/#feature" class="text-accent hover:underline"><code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">#feature</code></a> directive, which now errors if the feature is missing from this array.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-3">A third value, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">"vector"</code>, was accepted here until recently. It enabled nine builtin vector types (<code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">vec2f</code>…<code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">vec4h</code>) that no generator mapped and no runtime defined, so turning it on produced code that did not compile in any target. It has been <a href="/guides/directives/#feature" class="text-accent hover:underline">removed as unimplemented</a>. Remove it from <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">features</code> if your config still lists it — the config parser will now reject the file.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="generators" class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">generators</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3"><strong>Required.</strong> At least one generator must be configured. Each key is a target platform.</p>

      <h3 id="dotnet" class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">dotnet</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3">Generates C# code with multiple output files.</p>
      <div class="type-grid">
        <div class="type-grid-header">
          <span>Field</span>
          <span>Description</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-property">features</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Array of: <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">"models"</code> (type definitions), <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">"client"</code> (RPC client impls), <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">"server"</code> (server executors)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-property">outputs</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Output directory for generated files (relative to project root)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 id="browser" class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">browser</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3">Generates a single TypeScript file for browser clients.</p>
      <div class="type-grid">
        <div class="type-grid-header">
          <span>Field</span>
          <span>Description</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-property">outputFile</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Path to the generated <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">.ts</code> file</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-property">singleFileOutput</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Optional boolean. Folds the types and services of imported <a href="/guides/modules/" class="text-accent hover:underline">external modules</a> into the same <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">outputFile</code>.</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 id="rust" class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">rust</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3">Generates a Cargo crate: a <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Cargo.toml</code> in the output directory and all types, formatters and clients in <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">src/lib.rs</code> beneath it.</p>
      <div class="type-grid">
        <div class="type-grid-header">
          <span>Field</span>
          <span>Description</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-property">features</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Array of: <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">"models"</code> (type definitions), <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">"client"</code> (RPC client impls). There is no <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">"server"</code> — the Rust generator emits no server surface.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-property">outputs</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Crate root directory (relative to project root). Existing <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">.rs</code> files directly inside it are deleted before generation.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-property">crateName</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Optional. Cargo package name. Defaults to the project <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">name</code>, lowercased, with <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">.</code> replaced by <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">-</code>.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-property">rustcorePath</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Optional. Relative path to the <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">ion.rustcore</code> crate the generated code depends on, written into <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Cargo.toml</code> as a path dependency. Omitted, the dependency is taken from the registry instead.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="code-block text-[13px] mt-3">
        <pre>"rust": {'{'}
  "features": ["client"],
  "outputs": "./gen-rust",
  "crateName": "test-contracts",
  "rustcorePath": "../packages/ion.rustcore"
{'}'}</pre>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-6">Those three keys — <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">dotnet</code>, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">browser</code> and <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">rust</code> — are the whole set; any other platform key is rejected when the config is read. A fourth, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">"go"</code>, was accepted until recently. It has been <a href="/changelog/" class="text-accent hover:underline">removed</a>: there was no Go runtime in this repository, so nothing the Go generator emitted was ever compiled or verified. Remove the <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">"go"</code> block — and its <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">packageName</code> field — from <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">ion.config.json</code> if your config still lists it.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="modules" class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">modules</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3"><strong>Optional.</strong> A map of external module dependencies. Each key is the module name (used in <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">#import</code> directives), and the value is a relative path to the module's root directory:</p>
      <div class="code-block text-[13px]">
        <pre>"modules": {'{'}
  "auth": "../shared/auth-contracts",
  "common": "../shared/common-types"
{'}'}</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-3">Each referenced path must contain a valid <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">ion.config.json</code>. Modules are resolved recursively — if a module depends on other modules, those are resolved too. See the <a href="/guides/modules/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Modules guide</a> for details on resolution, cycle detection, and content hashing.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="validation" class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Validation</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">The <a href="#" class="text-accent hover:underline">IonPath Toolkit</a> VS Code extension provides JSON schema validation for <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">ion.config.json</code>. The schema is bundled at <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">extensions/ionpath-toolkit/schemas/ion-config.schema.json</code> and triggers automatically for any file named <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">ion.config.json</code>.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</DocsLayout>
